# ci-kueue-webhook-probe.service — one Kueue-webhook-endpoint-readiness gauge
# emission (see the .timer). Emitter for livespec-s43svm.46: catches the
# single-node, no-HA outage where kueue-webhook-service has ZERO ready endpoints,
# so the apiserver's mpod.kb.io admission call fails and every scale set's runner
# pods are silently rejected in `Initialize containers` — an outage that
# otherwise surfaces only as a misleading red content-check on an unrelated PR.
# Receiver: the CI-runner-host otel-collector (thewoolleyman/otel-collector
# config.ci-runner-host.yaml) on 127.0.0.1:4319, exporting to the `livespec`
# Honeycomb env. Paired trigger (filtered to this host.name): the value trigger
# fires when MAX(livespec.ci_kueue.webhook_ready_endpoints) < 1.
#
# Unlike the sibling ci-runner-heartbeat.service, this unit is NOT a DynamicUser:
# it runs as root so it can read the scoped, root-owned mode-0600 kubeconfig
# (CI_KUEUE_PROBE_KUBECONFIG) for the read-only ServiceAccount that is granted
# get,list on endpoints in kueue-system only.
# Source of truth: livespec-dev-tooling ci-runner/observability/ — install via
# install-observability.sh, never hand-edit the live copy (the s2t
# recreatability rule).
#
# BOOT ORDERING: the .timer's first tick fires ~2 min after boot, which on the
# reconstruct-on-boot path (livespec plan ci-runner-pod-lifecycle-reliability,
# boot-3 proof 2026-09-02 14:31Z) landed while converge-ci-stack.service was
# still installing Kueue and before otel-collector-identity.service had
# re-rendered the scoped kubeconfig, so the kubectl read failed and the probe
# exited 1 (correctly refusing to emit a false zero) — a red unit on every boot
# that the next tick heals, masking real failures from `systemctl --failed`.
# The After= below is ORDERING ONLY (no Requires=): a boot-time activation waits
# for the converged stack and the rendered kubeconfig; steady-state ticks are
# unaffected because those oneshots are already inactive by then.
[Unit]
Description=Kueue admission-webhook endpoint-readiness probe (OTLP gauge to local collector)
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target
After=k3s.service converge-ci-stack.service otel-collector-identity.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# Runs as root (default): needs to read the root-owned 0600 scoped kubeconfig.
ExecStart=/usr/local/lib/ci-runner/ci-kueue-webhook-probe.sh
